    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d184-a1">

                <pb facs="0361" n="243" sameAs="frus:frus1928v02/pg243"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 1]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Commander in Chief of the Asiatic Fleet</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bristol</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-06-13T16:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 13, 1928—4
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Following is being sent to the American Consul at Tientsin: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“June 13, 3 p.m. The Legation understands that there are a considerable
                            number of Americans at Peitaiho who have proceeded there in spite of
                            advices to the contrary. In view of the likelihood of their being
                            molested by retreating disorganized soldiery, some of whom may be unable
                            [to] proceed beyond Shanhaikuan, do you consider that Americans should
                            be advised to evacuate? Unless you consider it unnecessary, it is
                            suggested that you communicate with Commander-in-Chief, stating that
                            presence of a naval vessel either at Chinwangtao or off Peitaiho might
                            have a restraining effect. Legation is informed that British gunboat <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Foxglove</hi> is proceeding to Peitaiho. Are you
                            in communication with Peitaiho?”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
